direction: right
title: Java Concurrency & Thread Memory Architecture Overview

SharedMemory: Shared Process Memory (Heap/Metaspace) {
  style.fill: "#0B132B"
  style.stroke: "#0284C7"
  heap: "JVM Heap: Object instances, shared fields"
  metaspace: "Metaspace: Class bytecodes, static variables"
  jmm: "JMM: Happens-before ordering & memory barriers"
}

PlatformThreads: Platform Threads (1:1 OS Kernel) {
  style.fill: "#06201B"
  style.stroke: "#047857"
  stack: "1 MB dedicated OS stack per thread"
  cost: "Context switch: 1-2 microseconds"
  scale: "Max ~10,000 threads before OOM"
  best: "Ideal for CPU-bound computations"
}

VirtualThreads: Virtual Threads (M:N Loom) {
  style.fill: "#1E1B4B"
  style.stroke: "#8B5CF6"
  stack: "Dynamic continuation stack on Heap (few KB)"
  cost: "Context switch: 10-20 nanoseconds"
  scale: "Millions of threads concurrently"
  best: "Ideal for high-throughput I/O microservices"
}

SharedMemory -> PlatformThreads: JMM visibility & pointers
PlatformThreads -> VirtualThreads: Carriers execute virtual continuations
